{"images":[],"manifest":{"budgetTokens":15000,"countMethod":"proxy","model":"gpt-6-luna","packSha":"044a0466d050749c51c5e7244a27a2281ced23e38b8a745180f42b37e453e47b","packTokens":1321,"recipeVersion":"1","redactions":0,"sections":[{"id":"tpl","tokens":51,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"},{"id":"spans","tokens":162,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"answers","tokens":492,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"sentences","tokens":561,"trimmed":false,"trust":"derived"},{"id":"task","tokens":6,"trimmed":false,"trust":"trusted"}],"stage":"round-trip"},"pointers":[],"system":"Map each restated sentence to the original intent spans (I-n) and answers (Q-n) it comes from. A sentence that matches none gets empty lists. Every sentence n must appear once.","tools":[],"user":"<artifact id=\"spans\" kind=\"intent\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-1\",\n  \"text\": \"Build every operation of the locked API contract in contracts/openapi.yaml, exactly as it is written there.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-3\",\n  \"text\": \"Write its sample data in App.Api/SeedData.cs: a few believable rows for each table, taken from the contract's examples, so each list has something to show.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-4\",\n  \"text\": \"The app runs that file only when the setting Seed:Demo is true, so no test may count on those rows.\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"I-5\",\n  \"text\": \"The web app is built in its own repo; do not build screens here.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"answers\" kind=\"answers\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-1\",\n  \"question\": \"The product stories describe behaviors beyond the locked API contract, while the final instruction says to implement the contract exactly. When a story requires behavior the contract does not define, which scope should govern?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Implement only operations and behavior defined by the locked OpenAPI contract; do not add uncontracted behavior.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-2\",\n  \"question\": \"For sample rows that refer to one another, should the seeder create compatible references, or may it seed each table independently?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Create compatible references between related sample rows.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-3\",\n  \"question\": \"The contract includes an operation to return a configured staff identity-provider authorization URL, but the provider and source of that configuration are not identified here. What should the API use?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider and supply its authorization URL and token-validation settings through deployment configuration.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-4\",\n  \"question\": \"When demo seeding is disabled and a database table has no records, should list operations return an empty list or provide sample rows without persisting them?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Return an empty list when the database has no matching records.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n },\n {\n  \"id\": \"Q-5\",\n  \"question\": \"The staff identity-provider URL and token-validation settings will come from deployment configuration. What should happen if required settings are missing or invalid?\",\n  \"answer\": \"Fail application startup with a clear configuration error.\",\n  \"by\": \"Hamza (via web)\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\n<artifact id=\"sentences\" kind=\"restated\" sha=\"\">\n[\n {\n  \"n\": 1,\n  \"text\": \"Implement only the operations and behavior defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, retaining the existing root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes; conform to the contract for responses, filtering, authentication, authorization, and scope enforcement.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 2,\n  \"text\": \"Persist business-data changes to the configured PostgreSQL database, applying only lifecycle constraints stated in the contract; receipt creation must produce a Quarantined receipt, and valid customer order changes before packing must persist.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 3,\n  \"text\": \"Run `SeedData.Run` at startup when `Seed:Demo` is true; seed two to five contract-example-based rows only in empty contract-backed tables, preserve populated tables, and create valid references.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 4,\n  \"text\": \"When `Seed:Demo` is false or unset, do not run demo seeding or create demo rows; return empty lists for collections with no matching persisted records.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 5,\n  \"text\": \"Use the existing staff identity provider with deployment-configured authorization URL and token-validation settings, return that URL from the contracted operation, and validate staff tokens against those settings.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 6,\n  \"text\": \"Fail startup with an error identifying any missing or invalid required staff identity-provider setting, while allowing valid explicit settings in test and factory hosts.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 7,\n  \"text\": \"Authenticate customer accounts through the contract’s email-and-password and one-time-code flow, and authorize callers using roles, warehouse IDs, and organization IDs from the PostgreSQL account record matched to their authenticated email.\"\n },\n {\n  \"n\": 8,\n  \"text\": \"Apply ordered, versioned PostgreSQL schema migrations at startup, baseline compatible schemas created by the previous `EnsureCreated` startup, and preserve existing rows; fail startup without data loss when schema incompatibility cannot be migrated.\"\n }\n]\n</artifact>\n\nMap the sentences."}